  "title": "Flow through a rolling camera (golden, 9:16 carry across two orbits)",
  "notes": "Golden story for carry through camera moves that roll (docs/FLUID_MOTION_RFC.md \u00a76.6): three node-graph plates in one world-camera space, each turned 9 degrees from the last. The camera orbits to the second plate and back the other way to the third; with flow on from the steady feel, the title and hub ride a layer that cancels the camera's roll, so they stay upright and still on screen while the plates turn under them, and the cards glide from one fan into the next with the camera's own ease. No narration and no paid calls.",
